<h1>ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION AND SUSTAINABILITY POLICY</h1>

<p><strong>Organisation:</strong> Green Circular Lab (GBL)</p>
<p><strong>Policy area:</strong> Environmental Conservation and Climate Action</p>
<p><strong>Geographical scope:</strong> Uganda and GBL programme areas</p>
<p><strong>Policy status:</strong> Proposed, pending formal approval</p>

<div class="notice">
<strong>Our commitment:</strong>
GBL is committed to environmental responsibility, climate resilience,
sustainable resource use and protection of natural ecosystems.
</div>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
Green Circular Lab recognises the importance of protecting the
environment for present and future generations. Environmental
degradation, pollution, climate change, biodiversity loss and
unsustainable resource use threaten communities and development.
</p>
<p>
GBL seeks to promote practical environmental solutions through
education, innovation, technology, entrepreneurship and community
participation.
</p>

<h2>2. Purpose</h2>
<p>This policy aims to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Promote environmental conservation and responsible resource use.</li>
<li>Encourage climate change awareness and climate action.</li>
<li>Reduce pollution and unnecessary waste.</li>
<li>Support sustainable and circular economic practices.</li>
<li>Promote environmental education among young people and communities.</li>
<li>Encourage environmentally responsible organisational operations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Scope</h2>
<p>
This policy applies to GBL leadership, employees, volunteers,
interns, consultants, contractors, partners and all persons
participating in GBL activities.
</p>

<h2>4. Environmental Protection Principles</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Responsibility:</strong> Everyone should take responsibility for protecting the environment.</li>
<li><strong>Sustainability:</strong> Natural resources should be used responsibly.</li>
<li><strong>Prevention:</strong> Environmental damage should be prevented wherever reasonably possible.</li>
<li><strong>Participation:</strong> Communities should be involved in environmental decisions and activities.</li>
<li><strong>Innovation:</strong> Technology and creativity should support environmental solutions.</li>
<li><strong>Accountability:</strong> Environmental commitments should be monitored and reviewed.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Climate Change and Resilience</h2>
<p>
GBL supports awareness, education and practical initiatives that
help communities understand climate change and respond to its effects.
</p>
<p>Potential activities include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Climate change education and awareness campaigns.</li>
<li>Tree planting and restoration initiatives.</li>
<li>Community climate resilience education.</li>
<li>Promotion of renewable energy awareness.</li>
<li>Encouraging sustainable agriculture and land management.</li>
<li>Supporting locally appropriate environmental innovations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Waste Management and Circular Economy</h2>
<p>
GBL promotes responsible waste management and circular economy
principles that encourage resources to remain useful for longer.
</p>
<ul>
<li>Reduce unnecessary consumption.</li>
<li>Reuse materials whenever practical.</li>
<li>Separate waste where suitable facilities are available.</li>
<li>Promote recycling and responsible disposal.</li>
<li>Encourage repair and responsible product use.</li>
<li>Support community awareness about plastic pollution.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Biodiversity and Ecosystem Conservation</h2>
<p>
GBL supports the protection of biodiversity, forests, wetlands,
water resources, soil and other natural ecosystems.
</p>
<p>
Activities should respect local communities, applicable environmental
laws and the ecological needs of each project area.
</p>

<h2>8. Sustainable Organisational Operations</h2>
<p>GBL shall seek to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Use water and electricity responsibly.</li>
<li>Reduce unnecessary printing and paper consumption.</li>
<li>Promote digital communication where appropriate.</li>
<li>Avoid unnecessary single-use plastics.</li>
<li>Consider environmental impacts when purchasing supplies.</li>
<li>Dispose of electronic waste responsibly.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Environmental Education and Community Participation</h2>
<p>
GBL seeks to engage schools, youth, local communities, civil society
and other stakeholders in environmental learning and action.
</p>
<p>
Participation should be inclusive, respectful and responsive to
local environmental priorities.
</p>

<h2>10. Partnerships and Compliance</h2>
<p>
GBL will seek to collaborate with relevant government institutions,
educational institutions, environmental organisations, private
sector actors and development partners.
</p>
<p>
GBL activities should comply with applicable environmental laws,
regulations and relevant project requirements in Uganda.
</p>

<h2>11. Monitoring and Accountability</h2>
<p>
GBL will seek to monitor the environmental performance of its
activities through appropriate records, reviews and project reports.
</p>
<p>
Environmental concerns associated with GBL activities should be
reported to the organisation's authorised leadership for review
and appropriate action.
</p>

<h2>12. Review of the Policy</h2>
<p>
This policy should be reviewed periodically and updated when
necessary to reflect changes in environmental priorities,
organisational activities and applicable laws.
</p>

<h2>13. Approval and Authorisation</h2>

